# The QEMU driver without the stack (M9; user/root/src/net.rs and
# servers.rs; docs/design.md, "Network scenarios"). Root starts watch,
# uart and console, attaches as client 1, sets up PCI as test=net does
# (ECAM through carved device frames, virtio-net-pci at 00:02.0, its
# regions and MSI-X checked, the MSI bound to NV and MSI-X entry 0
# programmed, bus mastering on once the driver's frames are mapped,
# configuration space and the MSI-X table unmapped), and starts
# virtio-net (140) in a CSpace and VSpace of its own: its DMA frame, its
# three regions' device pages uncached, and the frame queues' frame. No
# net runs: a probe thread of root's own, at 130, in root's VSpace on a
# copy of the frame queues' frame, takes the link block, hands the driver
# every receive buffer, sends an ARP request for 10.0.2.2 built with
# net::arp, and waits for the reply, which libslirp sends from
# 52:55:0a:00:02:02. Root prints it, then the driver's Stats (frames each
# way, signals, no bad used element or queue entry) and passes.
cmdline: test=virtio_net
exit: success
nic: virtio-net
expect: root: cmdline "test=virtio_net"
expect: pci: ecam 0xe0000000, segment 0, buses 0-255
expect: pci: virtio-net at 00:02.0
expect: pci: virtio-net: MSI-X entry 0 sends IRQ
expect: bus mastering on; configuration space and the MSI-X table unmapped
expect: servers: virtio-net (priority 140, MSI-X IRQ
expect: probe (priority 130); root CNode
expect: virtio-net: up: MAC 52:54:00:12:34:56, features VERSION_1 MAC STATUS, link up, queues 64 and 64
expect: virtio_net: ARP reply: 10.0.2.2 is at 52:55:0a:00:02:02
expect: virtio-net: stats:
expect: , 0 bad used elements,
expect: , 0 bad queue entries,
expect: TEST PASS
expect: DEBUG HALT 0 from TCB
forbid: TEST FAIL
